      "id": 1,
      "text": "Hermann was founded by the German Settlement Society of Philadelphia in 1837.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hermann%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town is named after Hermann der Cherusker, the Germanic leader who defeated the Romans in 9 CE.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hermann%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Hermann has served as Gasconade County's seat since 1842 and remains the administrative hub of the county.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hermann%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By the early 1900s, Hermann boasted factories, with a shoe plant as the largest employer and other light industries thriving.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.gasconadecountyhistoricalsociety.com/hermann-missouri",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Hermann is the commercial center of the Hermann American Viticultural Area, where seven wineries produce about one‑third of Missouri's wine.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hermann%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Every year, Hermann hosts a Maifest on the third weekend of May and an Oktoberfest spanning the first four weekends of October.",
